<title>USA: St. Joe Corp Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>St. Joe Corp Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla. 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>ST. JOE CORPORATION</p>
<p>		 (Dollars in millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							 1996	 1995</p>
<p>Third Quarter:</p>
<p> Net sales and operating revenues	    $84.6     $82.9</p>
<p> Operating profit				    9.6	11.7</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations	    11.4	 6.4</p>
<p> Earnings from discontinued operations	  --	 4.8</p>
<p> Net income					   11.4	11.2</p>
<p>Per share amounts:</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations	    0.38	0.21</p>
<p> Earnings from discontinued operations	  --	0.16</p>
<p> Net income					   0.38	0.37</p>
<p>				    ST. JOE CORPORATION</p>
<p>		   (Dollars in millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							  1996     1995</p>
<p>Year to date:</p>
<p> Net sales and operating revenues	   $335.7   $245.2</p>
<p> Operating profit				  126.0     35.4</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations	    76.9     21.3</p>
<p> Earnings from discontinued operations	 0.7     37.7</p>
<p> Gain on sale of discontinued operations    90.4	 --</p>
<p> Net income					  168.0     59.0</p>
<p>Per share amounts:</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations	    2.53     0.70</p>
<p> Earnings from discontinued operations	0.02     1.23</p>
<p> Gain on sale of discontinued operations    2.96	 --</p>
<p> Net income					   5.51     1.93</p>
<p>1995 amounts have been restarted to reclassify the company's linerboard mill, container operations and communications segment as discontinued operations.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
